{"details":{"initial_reason":"object adds no factual detail beyond the subject","model_output_excerpt":"{\n  \"claim\": \"The People's Republic of China (PRC) is not a democracy, being an authoritarian one-party state led by the Chinese Communist Party (CCP)\",\n  \"relation\": \"attributed\",\n  \"object\": \"the PRC\",\n  \"evidence_text\": \"The People's Republic of China (PRC) is not a democracy, being an authoritarian one-party state led by the Chinese Communist Party (CCP)\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.98,\n  \"question_relevance\": \"direct\",\n  \"valid_from\": null,\n  \"valid_until\": null\n}","question":"What is the recognized as a republic of China?","reason":"object adds no factual detail beyond the subject","selected_passage_excerpt":"Debate over democracy in China has existed in Chinese politics since the 19th century.\nThe People's Republic of China (PRC) is not a democracy, being an authoritarian one-party state led by the Chinese Communist Party (CCP).\nCurrently, there are eight minor political parties in China other than the CCP that are legal, but all have to accept CCP primacy to exist.\nChina has been characterized as a dictatorship.\nFreedom of speech and freedom of assembly are severely restricted by the government.\nCensorship in China is widespread and dissent is harshly punished in the country.\nDemocracy movements in China have been repressed, most notably in the 1989 Tiananmen Square massacre.\nThe state constitution and CCP constitution both state that the PRC's form of government is \"people's democratic dictatorship\".\nUnder Xi Jinping's general secretaryship, China is also termed a \"whole-process people's democracy.\" The state constitution also holds that China is a one-party state that is governed by the CCP.","source_title":"Democracy in China","status":"ungrounded"},"event":"scholar.extraction_repair","ts_unix_ms":1791215751087}
