{"details":{"initial_reason":"subject terms are not sufficiently present in the evidence span","model_output_excerpt":"```json\n{\n  \"claim\": {\n    \"subject\": \"AI algorithms\",\n    \"relation\": \"is\",\n    \"object\": \"used as training data for AI models\",\n    \"evidence_text\": \"Large healthcare-related data warehouses of sometimes hundreds of millions of patients have been used as training data for AI models.\",\n    \"confidence\": 0.98,\n    \"question_relevance\": \"direct\",\n    \"valid_from\": null,\n    \"valid_until\": null\n  }\n}\n```","question":"How does AI assist in early detection of diseases in patients with limited access to healthcare?","reason":"subject terms are not sufficiently present in the evidence span","selected_passage_excerpt":"Section: Applications in healthcare systems\n\n## Applications in healthcare systems\n\n### Disease diagnosis\n\nAccurate and early diagnosis of diseases is still a challenge in healthcare.\nAI can assist clinicians with data processing capabilities to save time and improve accuracy.\nAI can help early prediction, for example, of Alzheimer's disease and dementias, by looking through large numbers of similar cases and possible treatments.\n\nIn 2023 a study reported higher satisfaction rates with ChatGPT-generated responses compared with those from physicians for medical questions posted on Reddit's r/AskDocs.\nMoreover, responses were not graded on the accuracy of medical information, and some have argued that the experiment was not properly blinded, with the evaluators being coauthors of the study.\n\nLarge healthcare-related data warehouses of sometimes hundreds of millions of patients have been used as training data for AI models.\n\nA 2025 meta-analysis in PLOS One found that the use of AI algorithms for detecting tooth decay was clinically justified.\n\n### Electronic health records\n\nAI algorithms have been created to evaluate individual patients' electronic health records, and to predict risks for diseases based on records and family histories.\nPhysicians do not have the bandwidth to process all this data manually, and AI can leverage this data to assist physicians in treating their patients.\nThese tools may also improve accessibility for patients synthesizing complex data, and writing responses in a desired conversational style or literacy level ultimately improving the overall efficiency of healthcare services.\n\n### AlphaFold and drug discovery\n\nAlphaFold has the ability to predict protein structures based on the constituent amino acid sequence, expected to have benefits in the life sciences—accelerating drug discovery and enabling better understanding of diseases.\nPivovarov and Elhada (2015) propose using wearable devices to allow for constant monitoring of a patient and the ability to notice changes via AI that may be less distinguishable by humans.\n\nA 2025 systematic review and meta-analysis of 15 studies comparing AI chatbots with human healthcare professionals in text-based consultations found that in a large majority of studies participants rated chatbot responses as more empathic than those from clinicians.\n\n### Workload management\n\nAI has the potential to streamline care coordination and reduce the workload.\nAI algorithms can automate administrative tasks, ","source_title":"Artificial intelligence in healthcare","status":"ungrounded"},"event":"scholar.extraction_repair","ts_unix_ms":1791217214015}
