{"details":{"initial_reason":"exact passage and claim term checks passed","initial_status":"accepted","model_output_excerpt":"```json\n{\"claim\":{\"subject\":\"Renewable energy\",\"relation\":\"is\",\"object\":\"energy which comes from natural resources such as sunlight, wind, rain, tides, and geothermal heat, which are renewable (naturally replenished)\",\"evidence_text\":\"Renewable energy is energy which comes from natural resources such as sunlight, wind, rain, tides, and geothermal heat, which are renewable (naturally replenished)\",\"confidence\":0.98,\"question_relevance\":\"direct\",\"valid_from\":null,\"valid_until\":null}}\n```","question":"How does the integration of renewable energy sources in urban planning contribute to long-term environmental and economic sustainability?","reason":"exact passage and claim term checks passed","relevance":"direct","selected_passage_excerpt":"This is a bibliography of renewable energy.\nRenewable energy is energy which comes from natural resources such as sunlight, wind, rain, tides, and geothermal heat, which are renewable (naturally replenished).\nAbout 16% of global final energy consumption comes from renewables, with 10% coming from traditional biomass, which is mainly used for heating, and 3.4% from hydroelectricity.\nNew renewables (small hydro, modern biomass, wind, solar, geothermal, and biofuels) account for another 3% and are growing very rapidly.\nTotal investment in renewable energy reached $244 billion in 2012.\nLeading renewable energy companies include BrightSource Energy, Enercon, First Solar, Gamesa, GE Energy, Goldwind, Nordex, Sinovel, Suntech, Trina Solar, Vestas and Yingli.","source_title":"List of books about renewable energy","status":"accepted"},"event":"scholar.extraction_decision","ts_unix_ms":1791217325963}
