{"details":{"evidence_match":{"method":"exact","original_passage_span":"Chicken pho is made using the same spices as beef, but the broth is made using chicken bones and meat, as well as some internal organs of the chicken, such as the heart, the undeveloped eggs, and the gizzard.","passage_byte_start":295,"proposed_evidence":"Chicken pho is made using the same spices as beef, but the broth is made using chicken bones and meat, as well as some internal organs of the chicken, such as the heart, the undeveloped eggs, and the gizzard.","proposed_evidence_chars":208},"initial_reason":"AI semantic entailment confirmed against original source quotation","initial_status":"accepted","model_output_excerpt":"{\"claim\":{\"subject\":\"Chicken pho\",\"relation\":\"is made using\",\"object\":\"the same spices as beef, but the broth is made using chicken bones and meat, as well as some internal organs of the chicken, such as the heart, the undeveloped eggs, and the gizzard.\",\"evidence_text\":\"Chicken pho is made using the same spices as beef, but the broth is made using chicken bones and meat, as well as some internal organs of the chicken, such as the heart, the undeveloped eggs, and the gizzard.\",\"confidence\":0.98,\"question_relevance\":\"direct\",\"valid_from\":null,\"valid_until\":null}}","question":"What is the typical preparation time for traditional chicken soup?","reason":"AI semantic entailment confirmed against original source quotation","relevance":"direct","review_guidance":null,"selected_passage_chars":2815,"selected_passage_excerpt":"Section: Ingredients and preparation\n\n## Ingredients and preparation\n\nWikibooks logo\nWikibooks Cookbook has a recipe/module on\n* ** Phở**\n\nPhở is served in a bowl with a specific cut of flat rice noodles in clear beef broth, with thin cuts of beef (steak, fatty flank, lean flank, brisket).\nChicken pho is made using the same spices as beef, but the broth is made using chicken bones and meat, as well as some internal organs of the chicken, such as the heart, the undeveloped eggs, and the gizzard.\n\nWhen eating at phở stalls in Vietnam, customers are generally asked which parts of the beef they would like and how they want it done.\n\nBeef parts include:\n* **Tái băm**: Rare beef patty, minced by a chopping knife right before serving\n* **Tái**: Medium rare meat\n* **Tái sống**: Rare meat\n* **Tái chín**: Mixture of medium rare meat and pre-cooked well-done meat, the default serving in most pho restaurants\n* **Tái lăn**: Meat, sauteed before adding to the soup\n* **Tái nạm**: Mix of medium rare meat with flank\n* **Nạm**: Flank cut\n* **Nạm gầu**: Brisket\n* **Gân**: Tendons\n* **Sách**: Beef tripe\n* **Tiết**: Boiled beef blood\n* **Bò viên**: Beef ball\n* **Trứng tái**: Poached chicken egg (served in a separate bowl)\n\nFor chicken phở, options might include:\n* **Đùi gà**: Chicken thigh\n* **Lườn gà**: Chicken breast\n* **Lòng gà**: Chicken innards\n* **Trứng non**: Immature chicken eggs\n* **Trứng chần:** chicken egg yolk\n\n### Noodles\n\nBags of bánh phở tươi at an Asian American grocery store\n\nThe freshly made rice noodles which are usually used are called bánh phở tươi, sợi phở tươi or for short, phở tươi in Vietnamese, while the dried rice noodles are called bánh phở khô, sợi phở khô or for short, phở khô.\nPho noodles are usually medium-wide; however, people from different regions of Vietnam prefer different widths.\n\n### Broth\n\nPhở served with beef brisket in Australia\n\nThe soup for beef phở is generally made by simmering beef bones, oxtails, flank steak, charred onion, charred ginger, and spices.\nChicken bones also work and produce a similar broth.\nFor chicken phở, only the meat and bones of the chicken are used in place of beef and beef bone.\nThe remaining spices remain the same, but the charred ginger can be omitted since its function in beef phở is to subdue the quite strong smell of beef.\n\nA typical phở spice packet, sold at many Asian food markets, containing a soaking bag plus various necessary dry spices.\nNước mắm (fish sauce) is added toward the end.\n\n### Garnishes\n\nTypical garnishes for phở Sài Gòn, clockwise from top left are: onions, chili peppers, culantro, lime, bean sprouts, and Thai basil.\n\nDifferent regions have different ways of eating pho that suit their taste and practice.\nThe Northern pho is typically served with scallions, onions, and cilantro (coriander leaves).","selected_passage_truncated":false,"semantic_support":{"evidence_text":"Chicken pho is made using the same spices as beef, but the broth is made using chicken bones and meat, as well as some internal organs of the chicken, such as the heart, the undeveloped eggs, and the gizzard.","model_verdict":"entailed","object":"the same spices as beef, but the broth is made using chicken bones and meat, as well as some internal organs of the chicken, such as the heart, the undeveloped eggs, and the gizzard.","reason":"The source passage explicitly states that Chicken pho is made using the same spices as beef, but the broth uses chicken bones and organs.","relation":"is made using","stance_override":null,"subject":"Chicken pho","valid_from":null,"valid_until":null,"verdict":"entailed"},"source_title":"Pho","status":"accepted"},"event":"scholar.extraction_decision","ts_unix_ms":1791231017579}
