+1⁄2 cup bowl of soup about 2,500 mg of sodium, a full day's allowance in the case of this mainstream brand.\nOther condensed chicken soups produced by Campbell's, such as Chicken with Rice or Chicken & Stars Soup, have similar amounts, as do generic versions of the product.\n\nCanned chicken soup with much less sodium than the traditional formulation is available, including many varieties produced by Campbell's, some with as little as 100 mg of sodium.\nCampbell's claims production of a chicken noodle soup that will find broad consumer acceptance—in short, that will sell—is very difficult, so it has to balance healthfulness with sodium content.\n\nUsually, the main ingredients of this canned soup are:\n* Chicken broth\n* Chicken\n* Noodles\n* Carrots\n* Salt\n* Celery, lettuce, or mushrooms, depending on the brand","selected_passage_truncated":false,"semantic_support":{"evidence_text":"Usually, the main ingredients of this canned soup are:\n* Chicken broth\n* Chicken\n* Noodles\n* Carrots\n* Salt\n* Celery, lettuce, or mushrooms, depending on the brand","model_verdict":"entailed","object":"a high-sodium product containing chicken broth, chicken, noodles, carrots, salt, and vegetables","reason":"The source explicitly lists chicken broth, chicken, noodles, carrots, salt, and vegetables as main ingredients of canned chicken soup.","relation":"is","stance_override":null,"subject":"Canned chicken soup","valid_from":null,"valid_until":null,"verdict":"entailed"},"source_title":"Chicken soup","status":"accepted"},"event":"scholar.extraction_decision","ts_unix_ms":1791231161927}
