{"details":{"evidence_match":{"method":"exact","original_passage_span":"In chemistry, the law of multiple proportions states that in compounds which contain two particular chemical elements, the amount of Element A per measure of Element B will differ across these compounds by ratios of small whole numbers.","passage_byte_start":0,"proposed_evidence":"In chemistry, the law of multiple proportions states that in compounds which contain two particular chemical elements, the amount of Element A per measure of Element B will differ across these compounds by ratios of small whole numbers.","proposed_evidence_chars":236},"initial_reason":"AI semantic entailment confirmed against original source quotation","initial_status":"accepted","model_output_excerpt":"```json\n{\n  \"claim\": {\n    \"subject\": \"Law of multiple proportions\",\n    \"relation\": \"states that\",\n    \"object\": \"in compounds which contain two particular chemical elements, the amount of Element A per measure of Element B will differ across these compounds by ratios of small whole numbers.\",\n    \"evidence_text\": \"In chemistry, the law of multiple proportions states that in compounds which contain two particular chemical elements, the amount of Element A per measure of Element B will differ across these compounds by ratios of small whole numbers.\",\n    \"confidence\": 0.98,\n    \"question_relevance\": \"direct\",\n    \"valid_from\": null,\n    \"valid_until\": null\n  }\n}\n```","question":"Find reliable evidence that supports, contradicts, or qualifies this assertion: Joseph Proust identified oxygen as the first element.","reason":"AI semantic entailment confirmed against original source quotation","relevance":"direct","review_guidance":null,"selected_passage_chars":860,"selected_passage_excerpt":"In chemistry, the law of multiple proportions states that in compounds which contain two particular chemical elements, the amount of Element A per measure of Element B will differ across these compounds by ratios of small whole numbers.\nThis law is also known as Dalton's Law, named after John Dalton, the chemist who first expressed it.\nThe discovery of this pattern led Dalton to develop the modern theory of atoms, as it suggested that the elements combine with each other in multiples of a basic quantity.\nFor example, if one tried to demonstrate it using the hydrocarbons decane (C10H22) and undecane (C11H24), one would find that 100 grams of carbon could react with 18.46 grams of hydrogen to produce decane or with 18.31 grams of hydrogen to produce undecane, for a ratio of hydrogen masses of 121:120, which is hardly a ratio of \"small\" whole numbers.","selected_passage_truncated":false,"semantic_support":{"evidence_text":"In chemistry, the law of multiple proportions states that in compounds which contain two particular chemical elements, the amount of Element A per measure of Element B will differ across these compounds by ratios of small whole numbers.","model_verdict":"entailed","object":"in compounds which contain two particular chemical elements, the amount of Element A per measure of Element B will differ across these compounds by ratios of small whole numbers.","reason":"The source passage explicitly states the law of multiple proportions, matching the candidate's subject and definition exactly.","relation":"states that","stance_override":null,"subject":"Law of multiple proportions","valid_from":null,"valid_until":null,"verdict":"entailed"},"source_title":"Law of multiple proportions","status":"accepted"},"event":"scholar.extraction_decision","ts_unix_ms":1791232785968}
