{"details":{"evidence_match":null,"initial_reason":"scholar returned invalid JSON: expected `,` or `}` at line 1 column 507","initial_status":"invalid_json","model_output_excerpt":"{\"claim\":{\"subject\":\"homemade chicken soup\",\"relation\":\"prep time\",\"object\":\"15 minutes\",\"evidence_text\":\"Homemade chicken soup that is, not out of a can. It's light, satisfying, heart warming and a remedy for colds and flu. If you're home over the weekend, think about making homemade soup. It's so simple. Gather the ingredients for the broth. I used a whole chicken, carrots, celery, onion, parsnips, parsley, and a bay leaf. Once you start cooking the broth, you're free to go do other things on your \"to do\" list. Check the broth once in awhile because you'll want to skim away any surface foam that forms on the top. After about 2 hours, the broth should be ready to become soup!\",\"confidence\":0.98,\"question_relevance\":\"direct\",\"valid_from\":null,\"valid_until\":null}}","question":"Homemade Whole Chicken Soup prep time 15 minutes","reason":"scholar returned invalid JSON: expected `,` or `}` at line 1 column 507","relevance":"unknown","review_guidance":null,"selected_passage_chars":726,"selected_passage_excerpt":"# Homemade Chicken Soup (hibernating recipes)\n\nPosted by Judy Matusky on December 7, 2017November 19, 2022\n\nWhat’s not to love about chicken soup? Homemade chicken soup that is, not out of a can. It’s light, satisfying, heart warming and a remedy for colds and flu. If you’re home over the weekend, think about making homemade soup. It’s so simple. Gather the ingredients for the broth. I used a whole chicken, carrots, celery, onion, parsnips, parsley, and a bay leaf. Once you start cooking the broth, you’re free to go do other things on your “to do” list. Check the broth once in awhile because you’ll want to skim away any surface foam that forms on the top. After about 2 hours, the broth should be ready to become soup!","selected_passage_truncated":false,