{"details":{"evidence_match":{"method":"whitespace_only","original_passage_span":"Remove the chicken from the soup pot and allow to cool.  Strain the broth, discarding the vegetables and return broth to pot.","passage_byte_start":453,"proposed_evidence":"Remove the chicken from the soup pot and allow to cool. Strain the broth, discarding the vegetables and return broth to pot.","proposed_evidence_chars":124},"initial_reason":"AI semantic entailment confirmed against original source quotation","initial_status":"accepted","model_output_excerpt":"{\"claim\":{\"subject\":\"Chicken\",\"relation\":\"is\",\"object\":\"a main ingredient in homemade whole chicken soup\",\"evidence_text\":\"Remove the chicken from the soup pot and allow to cool. Strain the broth, discarding the vegetables and return broth to pot.\",\"confidence\":0.98,\"question_relevance\":\"direct\",\"valid_from\":null,\"valid_until\":null}}","question":"Homemade Whole Chicken Soup prep time 15 minutes","reason":"AI semantic entailment confirmed against original source quotation","relevance":"direct","review_guidance":null,"selected_passage_chars":1047,"selected_passage_excerpt":"#### Directions\n1. Place chicken in a large soup pot. Stud onion halves with cloves and add them to the pot. Chop 3 celery stalks (with leaves if available), carrots and parsnips into 3 large pieces. Add them to the pot. Add garlic, dill, parsley and peppercorns. Add chicken broth and water until chicken and vegetables are covered by about an inch. Bring to a boil, reduce heat, cover and simmer for 2 hours. Occasionally skim off the foam on top.\n2. Remove the chicken from the soup pot and allow to cool.  Strain the broth, discarding the vegetables and return broth to pot. Bring the broth to a boil and cook uncovered for 10-15 minutes to intensify the flavor. Once chicken has cooled, remove skin and bones, discard. Shred the meat, place in a bowl, cover and set aside.\n3. Add 2 remaining celery stalks and 3 carrots, cut into 1/2 inch pieces. Cook uncovered until softened, about 10 minutes.\n4. Add peas and corn, dill, parsley, soy and Worcestershire sauce, chicken pieces and salt and pepper. Heat until soup is warm.\n\n*Judymatusky.com*","selected_passage_truncated":false,"semantic_support":{"evidence_text":"Remove the chicken from the soup pot and allow to cool.","model_verdict":"entailed","object":"a main ingredient in homemade whole chicken soup","reason":"Source explicitly states to remove chicken from the soup pot and return broth, confirming chicken is a main ingredient.","relation":"is","stance_override":null,"subject":"Chicken","valid_from":null,"valid_until":null,"verdict":"entailed"},"source_title":"Homemade Chicken Soup (hibernating recipes)","status":"accepted"},"event":"scholar.extraction_decision","ts_unix_ms":1791232928722}
