{"details":{"candidate":{"object":"zero-valence element","relation":"is a","subject":"Oganesson","valid_from":null,"valid_until":null},"model_output_excerpt":"{\"verdict\":\"entailed\",\"reason\":\"Source states Oganesson is a zero-valence element, matching the candidate relation.\",\"evidence_text\":\"Oganesson is a member of group 18, the zero-valence elements.\"}","model_verdict":"entailed","original_evidence":"Oganesson is a member of group 18, the zero-valence elements.","question":"Find reliable evidence that supports, contradicts, or qualifies this assertion: Oganesson subject of inquiry element with atomic number 118.","reason":"Source states Oganesson is a zero-valence element, matching the candidate relation.","source_title":"Oganesson","stance_override":null,"verdict":"entailed"},"event":"scholar.semantic_support","ts_unix_ms":1791233704431}
{"details":{"evidence_match":{"method":"exact","original_passage_span":"Oganesson is a member of group 18, the zero-valence elements.","passage_byte_start":99,"proposed_evidence":"Oganesson is a member of group 18, the zero-valence elements.","proposed_evidence_chars":61},"initial_reason":"AI semantic entailment confirmed against original source quotation","initial_status":"accepted","model_output_excerpt":"{\n  \"claim\": {\n    \"subject\": \"Oganesson\",\n    \"relation\": \"is a\",\n    \"object\": \"zero-valence element\",\n    \"evidence_text\": \"Oganesson is a member of group 18, the zero-valence elements.\",\n    \"confidence\": 0.98,\n    \"question_relevance\": \"direct\",\n    \"valid_from\": null,\n    \"valid_until\": null\n  }\n}","question":"Find reliable evidence that supports, contradicts, or qualifies this assertion: Oganesson subject of inquiry element with atomic number 118.","reason":"AI semantic entailment confirmed against original source quotation","relevance":"direct","review_guidance":"Extract the sentence stating the atomic number of oganesson to correct the claim.\nPrevious rejected claim: Oganesson is a zero-valence element\nPreferred exact evidence from reviewer: none","selected_passage_chars":1536,"selected_passage_excerpt":"Section: Calculated atomic and physical properties\n\n### Calculated atomic and physical properties\n\nOganesson is a member of group 18, the zero-valence elements.\nThe members of this group are usually inert to most common chemical reactions (for example, combustion) because the outer valence shell is completely filled with eight electrons.\nThis produces a stable, minimum energy configuration in which the outer electrons are tightly bound.\nIt is thought that similarly, oganesson has a closed outer valence shell in which its valence electrons are arranged in a 7s²7p⁶ configuration.\n\nConsequently, some expect oganesson to have similar physical and chemical properties to other members of its group, most closely resembling the noble gas above it in the periodic table, radon.\nFollowing the periodic trend, oganesson would be expected to be slightly more reactive than radon.\nIn addition to being far more reactive than radon, oganesson may be even more reactive than the elements flerovium and copernicium, which are heavier homologs of the more chemically active elements lead and mercury, respectively.\nThe reason for the possible enhancement of the chemical activity of oganesson relative to radon is an energetic destabilization and a radial expansion of the last occupied 7p-subshell.\nNevertheless, quantum electrodynamic corrections have been shown to be quite significant in reducing this affinity by decreasing the binding in the anion Og^{−} by 9%, thus confirming the importance of these corrections in superheavy elements.","selected_passage_truncated":false,"semantic_support":{"evidence_text":"Oganesson is a member of group 18, the zero-valence elements.","model_verdict":"entailed","object":"zero-valence element","reason":"Source states Oganesson is a zero-valence element, matching the candidate relation.","relation":"is a","stance_override":null,"subject":"Oganesson","valid_from":null,"valid_until":null,"verdict":"entailed"},"source_title":"Oganesson","status":"accepted"},"event":"scholar.extraction_decision","ts_unix_ms":1791233704431}
