{"details":{"evidence_match":{"method":"exact","original_passage_span":"The element with the highest atomic number known is oganesson (Z = 118), which completes the seventh period (row) in the periodic table.","passage_byte_start":102,"proposed_evidence":"The element with the highest atomic number known is oganesson (Z = 118), which completes the seventh period (row) in the periodic table.","proposed_evidence_chars":136},"initial_reason":"AI semantic entailment confirmed against original source quotation","initial_status":"accepted","model_output_excerpt":"{\n  \"claim\": {\n    \"subject\": \"Oganesson\",\n    \"relation\": \"is\",\n    \"object\": \"the element with the highest atomic number known\",\n    \"evidence_text\": \"The element with the highest atomic number known is oganesson (Z = 118), which completes the seventh period (row) in the periodic table.\",\n    \"confidence\": 0.98,\n    \"question_relevance\": \"direct\",\n    \"valid_from\": null,\n    \"valid_until\": null\n  }\n}","question":"Find reliable evidence that supports, contradicts, or qualifies this assertion: Oganesson subject of inquiry element with atomic number 118.","reason":"AI semantic entailment confirmed against original source quotation","relevance":"direct","review_guidance":"Find a source that directly addresses the atomic number of Oganesson.","selected_passage_chars":1192,"selected_passage_excerpt":"An extended periodic table theorizes about chemical elements beyond those currently known and proven.\nThe element with the highest atomic number known is oganesson (Z = 118), which completes the seventh period (row) in the periodic table.\nAll elements in the eighth period and beyond thus remain purely hypothetical.\nElements beyond 118 would be placed in additional periods when discovered, laid out (as with the existing periods) to illustrate periodically recurring trends in the properties of the elements.\nAny additional periods are expected to contain more elements than the seventh period, as they are calculated to have an additional so-called g-block, containing at least 18 elements with partially filled g-orbitals in each period.\nAn eight-period table containing this block was suggested by Glenn T.\nThe first element of the g-block may have atomic number 121, and thus would have the systematic name unbiunium.\nDespite many searches, no elements in this region have been synthesized or discovered in nature.\nAccording to the orbital approximation in quantum mechanical descriptions of atomic structure, the g-block would correspond to elements with partially filled g-orbitals...","selected_passage_truncated":false,"semantic_support":{"evidence_text":"The element with the highest atomic number known is oganesson (Z = 118), which completes the seventh period (row) in the periodic table.","model_verdict":"entailed","object":"the element with the highest atomic number known","reason":"The source explicitly states the element with the highest atomic number known is oganesson (Z = 118), matching the candidate's subject.","relation":"is","stance_override":null,"subject":"Oganesson","valid_from":null,"valid_until":null,"verdict":"entailed"},"source_title":"Extended periodic table","status":"accepted"},"event":"scholar.extraction_decision","ts_unix_ms":1791233792294}
